This change keeps first attribute names in-line with the element and indented to align to other attributes where possible, i.e. when the element name is 3 characters or less (for 4-character indentation). Addresses #22.

```rust
html! {
    p   class="short element name on same line but indented"
        href="#" 
        data-bloat="aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
    { "link" }
    section
        class="long element name on next line"
        href="#" 
        data-bloat="aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
    { "link" }
}

// compare to current behaviour:

html! {
    p
        class="short element name but pushed to next line"
        href="#" 
        data-bloat="aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
    { "link" }
}
```

